'============================================================
' Example 2: Variable Scope and Function/Sub Copy-Back
'
' CRBasic's scope and parameter-passing rules differ from most
' languages:
'   - A Public variable is ALWAYS global, even when the Public
'     statement appears inside a Sub or Function body.
'   - Function parameters are copied in but never copied back:
'     the caller's variable is unchanged after the call returns.
'   - Sub parameters ARE copied back: the caller's variable is
'     updated when the Sub returns, like a by-reference argument.
'
' Try it in the editor:
'   - Go to Definition on RunningTotal from inside AddSample.
'   - Find All References on RunningTotal from its declaration.
'   - Hover over Function and Sub for the copy-back documentation.
'============================================================

Dim Sample1
Dim Sample2

' Doubles its argument locally; the caller's variable is
' untouched after the call returns.
Function Doubled(value)
  value = value * 2
  Doubled = value
EndFunction

' RunningTotal is declared Public here, inside the Sub body --
' it is still a global variable, not local to AddSample.
Sub AddSample(amount)
  Public RunningTotal
  RunningTotal = RunningTotal + amount
  amount = amount * 2 ' copied back to the caller on return
EndSub

BeginProg
  Sample1 = 10
  Sample2 = Doubled(Sample1) ' Sample1 stays 10; Sample2 becomes 20

  AddSample(Sample1) ' RunningTotal accumulates; Sample1 becomes 20
EndProg
